# Text files are stored and checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' default `core.autocrlf=true` checks text out
# with CRLF, and `include_str!` of the repository's own data (minigames/*.toml,
# tests/data/*.toml, tools/testmap/*.vmf, specs) then holds CRLF where the code
# and tests expect LF. The fast tier failed seven tests on a plain Windows
# clone for that reason: their `.replace("...\n...", "...")` calls silently
# matched nothing, so the rule lines they add never reached the minigame text
# and the ammo table they remove stayed in the document.
#
# An existing clone keeps its CRLF files until it is checked out again:
#   git rm -r --cached . && git reset --hard
* text=auto eol=lf
